{"entries":[{"id":"tsk-hab-1-intro","title":"Habakkuk 1 — Chapter Introduction","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"HAB","chapterStart":1,"verseStart":0,"chapterEnd":1,"verseEnd":0},"content":"<p>I am. 3:5; Jer 21:13; 50:31; 51:25; Eze 5:8; 26:3; 28:22; 29:3,10 Eze 35:3; 38:3; 39:1 I will burn. Jos 11:9; 2Ki 19:23; Ps 46:9 and the sword. Isa 31:8,9; 37:36-38 I will cut. 3:1,12; Isa 33:1-4; 49:24,25 the voice. 2Ki 18:17,19,27-35; 19:9,23; 2Ch 32:9-16,19</p>"},{"id":"tsk-hab-1-1","title":"Habakkuk 1:1","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"HAB","chapterStart":1,"verseStart":1,"chapterEnd":1,"verseEnd":1},"content":"<p>1 Unto Habakkuk, complaining of the iniquity of the land, 5 is shewn the fearful vengeance by the Chaldeans. 12 He complains that vengeance should be executed by them who are far worse.</p>\n<p>Isa 22:1; Na 1:1</p>"},{"id":"tsk-hab-1-2","title":"Habakkuk 1:2","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"HAB","chapterStart":1,"verseStart":2,"chapterEnd":1,"verseEnd":2},"content":"<p>how. Ps 13:1,2; 74:9,10; 94:3; Re 6:10 and thou wilt not save. Ps 22:1,2; Jer 14:9; La 3:8</p>"},{"id":"tsk-hab-1-3","title":"Habakkuk 1:3","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"HAB","chapterStart":1,"verseStart":3,"chapterEnd":1,"verseEnd":3},"content":"<p>Ps 12:1,2; 55:9-11; 73:3-9; 120:5,6; Ec 4:1; 5:8; Jer 9:2-6; Eze 2:6 Mic 7:1-4; Mt 10:16; 2Pe 2:8</p>"},{"id":"tsk-hab-1-4","title":"Habakkuk 1:4","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"HAB","chapterStart":1,"verseStart":4,"chapterEnd":1,"verseEnd":4},"content":"<p>the law. Ps 11:3; 119:126; Mr 7:9; Ro 3:31 for. 1Ki 21:13; Job 21:7; Ps 22:16; 58:1,2; 59:2,4; 82:1-5; 94:3,20,21 Isa 1:21-23; 59:2-8,13-15; Jer 5:27-29; 12:1,6; 26:8,21-23 Jer 37:14-16; 38:4-6; Eze 22:25-30; Ho 10:4; Am 5:7,12; Mic 2:1,2 Mic 3:1-3; 7:2-4; Mt 23:34-36; 26:59-66; 27:1,2,25,26; Ac 7:52,59 Ac 23:12-14; Jas 2:6,7 wrong. or, wrested. Ex 23:2,6; De 16:19; Eze 9:9</p>"},{"id":"tsk-hab-1-5","title":"Habakkuk 1:5","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"HAB","chapterStart":1,"verseStart":5,"chapterEnd":1,"verseEnd":5},"content":"<p>ye among. De 4:27; Jer 9:25,26; 25:14-29 and regard. Isa 29:14; La 4:12; Da 9:12; Ac 13:40,41 for. Isa 28:21,22; Jer 5:12,13; 18:18; Eze 12:22-28; Zep 1:2; Ac 6:13,14</p>"},{"id":"tsk-hab-1-6","title":"Habakkuk 1:6","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"HAB","chapterStart":1,"verseStart":6,"chapterEnd":1,"verseEnd":6},"content":"<p>I raise. De 28:49-52; 2Ki 24:2; 2Ch 36:6,17; Isa 23:13; 39:6,7; Jer 1:15,16 Jer 4:6,8; 5:15; 6:22,23; 21:4; 25:9 breadth. Heb. breadths.</p>"},{"id":"tsk-hab-1-7","title":"Habakkuk 1:7","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"HAB","chapterStart":1,"verseStart":7,"chapterEnd":1,"verseEnd":7},"content":"<p>their judgment, etc. or, from them shall proceed the judgmentof these and the captivity of these. Jer 39:5-9; 52:9-11,25-27; De 5:19,27</p>"},{"id":"tsk-hab-1-8","title":"Habakkuk 1:8","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"HAB","chapterStart":1,"verseStart":8,"chapterEnd":1,"verseEnd":8},"content":"<p>horses. De 28:49; Isa 5:26-28 fierce. Heb. sharp. evening. Jer 5:6; Zep 3:3 they. Jer 4:13; La 4:19; Eze 17:3,12; Ho 8:1; Mt 24:28; Lu 17:37</p>"},{"id":"tsk-hab-1-9","title":"Habakkuk 1:9","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"HAB","chapterStart":1,"verseStart":9,"chapterEnd":1,"verseEnd":9},"content":"<p>for. 6; 2:5-13; De 28:51,52; Jer 4:7; 5:15-17; 25:9 their faces shall sup up as the east. or, the supping up oftheir faces, as, etc. or, their faces shall look toward the east. Heb. the opposition of their faces shall be toward the east. Isa 27:8; Jer 4:11; Eze 17:10; 19:12; Ho 13:15 they shall gather. 2:5; Ge 41:49; Jud 7:12; Job 29:18; Ps 139:18; Jer 15:8; 34:22 Ho 1:10; Ro 9:27</p>"},{"id":"tsk-hab-1-10","title":"Habakkuk 1:10","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"HAB","chapterStart":1,"verseStart":10,"chapterEnd":1,"verseEnd":10},"content":"<p>scoff. 2Ki 24:12; 25:6,7; 2Ch 36:6,10 they shall deride. Isa 14:16; Jer 32:24; 33:4; 52:4-7</p>"},{"id":"tsk-hab-1-11","title":"Habakkuk 1:11","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"HAB","chapterStart":1,"verseStart":11,"chapterEnd":1,"verseEnd":11},"content":"<p>shall his. Da 4:30-34 imputing. Da 5:3,4,20</p>"},{"id":"tsk-hab-1-12","title":"Habakkuk 1:12","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"HAB","chapterStart":1,"verseStart":12,"chapterEnd":1,"verseEnd":12},"content":"<p>thou not. De 33:27; Ps 90:2; 93:2, Isa 40:28; 57:15; La 5:19; Mic 5:2 1Ti 1:17; 6:16; Heb 1:10-12; 13:8; Re 1:8,11 mine. Isa 43:15; 49:7; Ac 3:14 we. 3:2; Ps 118:17; Isa 27:6-9; Jer 4:27; 5:18; 30:11; 33:24-26; 46:28 Eze 37:11-14; Am 9:8,9 thou hast ordained. 2Ki 19:25; Ps 17:13; Isa 10:5-7; 37:26; Jer 25:9-14; Eze 30:25 mighty God. Heb. Rock. De 32:4,30,31; 1Sa 2:2; Ps 18:1 established. Heb. founded. for. Isa 27:9,10; Jer 30:11; 31:18-20; 46:28; Heb 12:5,6</p>"},{"id":"tsk-hab-1-13","title":"Habakkuk 1:13","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"HAB","chapterStart":1,"verseStart":13,"chapterEnd":1,"verseEnd":13},"content":"<p>of. Job 15:15; Ps 5:4,5; 11:4-7; 34:15,16; 1Pe 1:15,16 iniquity. or, grievance. wherefore. Ps 10:1,2,15; 73:3; Jer 12:1,2 deal. Isa 21:2; 33:1 holdest. Es 4:14; Ps 35:22; 50:3,21; 83:1; Pr 31:8,9; Isa 64:12 the wicked. 3,4; 2Sa 4:11; 1Ki 2:32; Ps 37:12-15,32,33; 56:1,2; Ac 2:23; 3:13-15</p>"},{"id":"tsk-hab-1-14","title":"Habakkuk 1:14","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"HAB","chapterStart":1,"verseStart":14,"chapterEnd":1,"verseEnd":14},"content":"<p>creeping. or, moving. no. Pr 6:7</p>"},{"id":"tsk-hab-1-15","title":"Habakkuk 1:15","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"HAB","chapterStart":1,"verseStart":15,"chapterEnd":1,"verseEnd":15},"content":"<p>take. Jer 16:16; Eze 29:4,5; Am 4:2; Mt 17:27 they catch. Ps 10:9; Lu 5:5-10; Joh 21:6-11 drag. or, flue-net. therefore. Jer 50:11; La 2:15,16; Eze 25:6; 26:2; 35:15; Re 11:10</p>"},{"id":"tsk-hab-1-16","title":"Habakkuk 1:16","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"HAB","chapterStart":1,"verseStart":16,"chapterEnd":1,"verseEnd":16},"content":"<p>they. 11; De 8:17; Isa 10:13-15; 37:24; Eze 28:3; 29:3; Da 4:30; 5:23 plenteous. or, dainty. Heb. fat.</p>"},{"id":"tsk-hab-1-17","title":"Habakkuk 1:17","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"HAB","chapterStart":1,"verseStart":17,"chapterEnd":1,"verseEnd":17},"content":"<p>and. 9,10; 2:5-8,17; Isa 14:16,17; Jer 25:9-26; 46:1-49:39; 52:1-34 Eze 25:1-30:26</p>"}]}